usage: author_chapter.py [-h] --brief BRIEF --sources SOURCES --output OUTPUT
                         --receipt RECEIPT --chapter CHAPTER

Owner-side execution helper; publishing remains the app's ordinary API/MCP.

Calls only the pinned author route. When a draft fails the mechanical checks the
helper itself asks the same pinned route again with the check's error (at most
two more times, inside one shared budget). Only an accepted draft becomes a
chapter file and receipt. Rejected drafts go to `rejected/` beside the receipt,
wrapped as rejected evidence; they are never an edition.

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  --brief BRIEF
  --sources SOURCES
  --output OUTPUT
  --receipt RECEIPT
  --chapter CHAPTER
AUTHOR-CHAPTER-HELP-EXIT=0
usage: author_collection.py [-h]
                            {export,install,revision-preview,revision-apply}
                            ...

Owner-side, new-collection-only bridge. Never modifies the reader or donor.
Uses the existing version-1 library importer as the final document validator.
No authoring jobs, provider calls, revisions, deletions or automatic
activation.

positional arguments:
  {export,install,revision-preview,revision-apply}
    export              Export exactly one new collection
    install             Stage by default; enabling requires explicit --enable
    revision-preview    Stage exact existing-collection revision; does not
                        apply
    revision-apply      Explicitly apply a saved exact preview

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
AUTHOR-COLLECTION-HELP-EXIT=0
